  "text": "I'll review the round-11 fixes against the ship bar, starting with the synthesis, the spec, and the new verify/push code.Round 11's synthesis and the new verify/push path are the first things to check. I'll read those, then try the old repros against HEAD.Round 11's fix is `6c13414`, under the sandbox commit. I'll read that diff and the push and verify paths next.The new layout check and the push denylist are the places a redirect could still slip through. I'll probe ref links, the index, and repo-local push settings against HEAD.The ref symlink was one directory too high, so the probe died early. I'll fix that and keep going if one case fails.The proxy probe was written and never run. I'll execute it, then the Publish regression tests, before the ship call.Round 11's layout check is in place. Next I'll test the variants it doesn't cover: an in-admin index alias, `remote.origin.proxy` on a literal URL, and submodule recursion.`remote.origin.proxy` does not steer a literal URL. The next check is whether git normalizes a path before `pushInsteadOf` in a way the prefix check misses. The submodule fixture's bare HEAD was unborn; I'll fix that and rerun.Publish's push sets `GIT_DIR`, so recursion stayed off. `core.worktree` pointing at the pane gives that push a work tree and may turn it back on. I'll test that.SHIP \u2014 round 11's layout check, lock recheck, and push-unknown handling hold. The isolated suite is 348 tests, OK. Nothing proven meets the ship bar.\n\n## BLOCKING FINDINGS\n\nNone.\n\n## NON-BLOCKING\n\n- A pane index symlinked straight at the main index: the agent's own `git add` rewrites that index, then `verify` raises `IdentityError` (`worktrees.py:939`). An in-admin symlink whose target is a hardlink of the main index still passes `verify`; `git add` replaces the link and leaves the main index unchanged. `scratch/probe_r12e.py`.\n- `remote.<name>.proxy` is outside `_TRANSPORT_KEYS` (`worktrees.py:1516`). On git 2.55 a literal URL push still connects to the confirmed host; `http.proxy` connects to the proxy and is refused. Same probe.\n- `pushInsteadOf` rewrites a literal URL only when the confirmed string already starts with the configured prefix (trailing slash included). `foo/../`, a doubled slash, a symlink directory, and `file://` versus a path do not cross-rewrite. `scratch/probe_r12g.py`.\n- `git remote get-url --push` applies a global `pushInsteadOf`, so the dialog shows the rewritten URL and Publish pushes that URL. A repo-local `url.*` / `http.*` / `include.*` still refuses Publish, including harmless keys.\n- A submodule added after create, with `push.recurseSubmodules=on-demand` and `core.worktree` set to the pane: `verify` passes, `transport_override` is empty, and `push()` returns success for the confirmed superproject URL. The submodule commit is not delivered (`cd to 'sub' failed`, exit 0). The pane's own `git push`, outside `GIT_DIR`, does push that submodule to the retargeted URL. `scratch/probe_r12f.py`, `scratch/probe_r12h.py`.\n- `push.recurseSubmodules=only` can make `git push` exit 0 without updating the confirmed remote; the op is recorded `unknown` until `corral-light worktrees resolve --op`.\n- `BugBash6Publish.test_BB6_13` (`test_worktrees.py:3394`) accepts reason `rewrite` or `transport`, so a broken insteadOf parser still passes while repo-local `url.*` is refused as transport. `BB6_14` covers a global `pushInsteadOf` and passed.\n- `open_pr` (`worktrees.py:1735`) passes the client's `pr.repo` to `gh pr create --repo`. The UI sends the snapshot's `githubRepo` (`static/app.js:1569`). A crafted POST can open the PR on another repo after the push has gone to the confirmed URL.\n\nAn agent that checks out any other branch locks that pane, Discard included, until someone switches `corral/<slug>` back.",
